            </font>

        </td></tr>
        <tr id="comment-body-620555"><td bgcolor="#ffffff">
            <p>I updated the RFC description. </p>

<ul>
	<li>Prompt Processing has turned on lossy compression at prompt output generation for all 3 image types since about 1 month ago. The size in this RFC is updated for the compressed size. </li>
</ul>


<ul>
	<li>The heaviest type  <tt>template_detector</tt> is moved from Tier 1 to Tier 2 per popular demand. </li>
</ul>


<ul>
	<li>Notes are added about future consideration re: dataset consolidation and non-realtime pipelines. I mean this RFC to provide a baseline before work on consolidation and non-realtime pipeline is ready for production.  </li>
</ul>


<p>The total size has dropped significantly. </p>
        </td></tr>
                <tr id="comment-header-620757"><td bgcolor="#f0f0f0">
            Comment by  
                                                    
                
        
            <a class="user-hover" rel="712020:34995da4-22f6-4b5f-9b25-34bff6b9b0e6"
                id="word_commented_712020:34995da4-22f6-4b5f-9b25-34bff6b9b0e6"
                href="https://rubinobs.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=712020%3A34995da4-22f6-4b5f-9b25-34bff6b9b0e6">
                    Hsin-Fang Chiang
                </a>

                                        <font size="-2">
            [
                <font color="#336699">07/Jan/26</font>

                            ]
            </font>

        </td></tr>
        <tr id="comment-body-620757"><td bgcolor="#ffffff">
            <p>I missed two dataset types that are pipeline init outputs: <tt>single_visit_star_schema</tt>  and <tt>dia_source_schema</tt> .  There is only one of each per day per pipeline per deployment and they are small (&lt;100KB each). </p>

<p>Questions to the Pipelines folks: should we include them in the publication?  </p>
        </td></tr>
                <tr id="comment-header-620774"><td bgcolor="#f0f0f0">
