        <tr id="comment-body-624816"><td bgcolor="#ffffff">
            <p>Apologies for reopening this. </p>

<p>As Daytime AP catchup campaign is ramping up, it might be easier to consider the additional types together.  The Daytime AP catchup runs additional pipelines besides what realtime prompt processing runs; notably `consolidateVisitSummary` and `singleFrameDetectAndMeasure` (after 
    <span class="jira-issue-macro resolved" data-jira-key="DM-53893" >
                <a href="https://rubinobs.atlassian.net/browse/DM-53893" class="jira-issue-macro-key issue-link"  title="Move SingleFrameDetectAndMeasure into Daytime AP pipeline" >
            <img class="icon" src="https://rubinobs.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/universal_avatar/view/type/issuetype/avatar/10318?size=medium" />
            DM-53893
        </a>
                                                    <span class="aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-subtle aui-lozenge-success jira-macro-single-issue-export-pdf">Done</span>
            </span>
). They add two additional types `preliminary_visit_summary` and `single_visit_star_reprocessed_footprints` ; we want to keep both until DR1 (promised in RTN-011) </p>

<p>Also for clarity I separated out in a different tier the solar system catalog types that should not be necessary once PPDB is available. </p>

<p><a href="https://rubinobs.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=557058%3A5afef4b4-f1bc-4238-977f-9f8d3183e55c" class="user-hover" rel="557058:5afef4b4-f1bc-4238-977f-9f8d3183e55c" data-account-id="557058:5afef4b4-f1bc-4238-977f-9f8d3183e55c" accountid="557058:5afef4b4-f1bc-4238-977f-9f8d3183e55c" rel="noreferrer">Gregory Dubois-Felsmann</a> please take a look. </p>
        </td></tr>
