                    Ian Sullivan
                </a>

                                        <font size="-2">
            [
                <font color="#336699">23/Jan/26</font>

                            ]
            </font>

        </td></tr>
        <tr id="comment-body-624819"><td bgcolor="#ffffff">
            <p><a href="https://rubinobs.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=5c2f5797a217aa69bce53f54" class="user-hover" rel="5c2f5797a217aa69bce53f54" data-account-id="5c2f5797a217aa69bce53f54" accountid="5c2f5797a217aa69bce53f54" rel="noreferrer">Jim Bosch</a> We could use <tt>single_visit_star_reprocessed_unstandardized</tt> as the equivalent Parquet file to the <tt>_footprints</tt> catalog. To my knowledge we don’t have an equivalent of the 5-sigma direct source catalogs produced by AP in <tt>sdm_schemas</tt>, so there isn’t currently a standardized version. If we define one it would be easy to add a standardization step to the Daytime AP pipeline.</p>
        </td></tr>
                <tr id="comment-header-624934"><td bgcolor="#f0f0f0">
            Comment by  
                                                    
                
        
            <a class="user-hover" rel="5c2f5797a217aa69bce53f54"
