        <tr id="comment-body-625297"><td bgcolor="#ffffff">
            <p>If I understood <a href="https://rubinobs.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=557058%3A5afef4b4-f1bc-4238-977f-9f8d3183e55c" class="user-hover" rel="557058:5afef4b4-f1bc-4238-977f-9f8d3183e55c" data-account-id="557058:5afef4b4-f1bc-4238-977f-9f8d3183e55c" accountid="557058:5afef4b4-f1bc-4238-977f-9f8d3183e55c" rel="noreferrer">Gregory Dubois-Felsmann</a>  correctly, per-detector is preferable from an RSP perspective? <br/>
But from the Pipelines perspective and infrastructure perspective, per-visit might be preferable, so to be analogous to the DRP <tt>source</tt> and to occupy fewer rows in the database? </p>
        </td></tr>
