        </td></tr>
        <tr id="comment-body-625518"><td bgcolor="#ffffff">
            <p>A couple of comments on this thread:</p>

<ul>
	<li>I would definitely want a representation of the schema in sdm_schemas, and the data to be in the “VOParquet” format.</li>
	<li>Regarding visit vs. visit-detector: as I noted on Slack, I would be OK with visit dimensions if the Parquet file had the detectors as indexed row groups.  We would very much like to be able to load one detector’s sources efficiently, whether that’s done directly in the Butler (in analogy with the way we handle zipped raws) or as something that we do “by hand” reading from a deferred-dataset-handle.</li>
</ul>


<p>As quantitative grist for the mill, could we get an estimate of the range for the number of rows we’re likely to see per detector, between sparse extragalactic fields and crowded MW fields?</p>
        </td></tr>
                <tr id="comment-header-625519"><td bgcolor="#f0f0f0">
