        <tr id="comment-body-625521"><td bgcolor="#ffffff">
            <p><a href="https://rubinobs.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=557058%3A20ad3b56-9b88-4b76-bb4e-576e831f79ae" class="user-hover" rel="557058:20ad3b56-9b88-4b76-bb4e-576e831f79ae" data-account-id="557058:20ad3b56-9b88-4b76-bb4e-576e831f79ae" accountid="557058:20ad3b56-9b88-4b76-bb4e-576e831f79ae" rel="noreferrer">William O'Mullane</a> My understanding is that <tt>single_visit_star_reprocessed_footprints</tt> is mostly for the measurements; the actual footprints might be removed from the catalog as it is standardized into <tt>ap_source</tt>, which might reduce the size a lot.</p>
